240
00:15:10,281 --> 00:15:17,060
The Batsuit's flexible, armor-plated design parallels an actual technology called ceramic armor,

241
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:21,440
made by companies like Ceradyn Incorporated in Costa Mesa, California.

242
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:28,120
Their ceramic plating has the resistance of steel, the material that's long been used to stop bullets.

243
00:15:28,820 --> 00:15:31,720
But ceramic plating is 70% lighter.

244
00:15:32,620 --> 00:15:35,020
To stop the bullet, you have to break the bullet.

245
00:15:35,660 --> 00:15:38,920
Therefore, you need something that is harder than the bullet.

246
00:15:38,921 --> 00:15:46,980
The lightest weight, hardest material known to man for these types of applications is known as boron carbide.

247
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:50,260
Boron carbide is a black crystalline powder.

248
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:57,340
When heated to extreme temperatures and formed into ceramic plating, it becomes nearly as hard as diamonds.

249
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:01,500
So where you are right now are in the hot pressing area.

250
00:16:01,980 --> 00:16:07,760
This is where we take a powder and we make it into the lightest, hardest material known to man.

251
00:16:07,761 --> 00:16:12,660
Transforming the particles into armor begins by pouring the powder into forms

252
00:16:12,661 --> 00:16:18,080
and then compressing the material. The armor molds are then put into a hot press.

253
00:16:18,081 --> 00:16:22,102
And behind me you can see the hot presses.

254
00:16:22,103 --> 00:16:26,220
These are induction heated and they operate

255
00:16:26,221 --> 00:16:30,080
at temperatures close to 4,000 degrees Fahrenheit.

256
00:16:30,081 --> 00:16:35,260
The plates are then cooled but they're not safe to be used as armor yet.

257
00:16:35,261 --> 00:16:39,800
In certain high impacts, ceramic armor plating still will shatter.

258
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:43,880
But that's actually a benefit because it really dissipates the energy

259
00:16:43,881 --> 00:16:46,560
into the shattering of the material instead of your body.

260
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:52,160
But shards of shattered ceramic plating can still be deadly if they enter the body.

261
00:16:52,780 --> 00:16:54,680
To prevent this lethal possibility,

262
00:16:55,200 --> 00:17:00,120
a special resin is fused to the back of each piece of armor to catch the broken shards.

263
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:03,340
The final step is we have to put out an outer layer.

264
00:17:03,341 --> 00:17:05,840
The outer layer is called the spall shield.

265
00:17:05,841 --> 00:17:12,140
So when a bullet comes in, not only do you stop it and catch the fragments in the back,

266
00:17:12,141 --> 00:17:15,840
but there may be a little bit that tends to fly in the wrong direction.

267
00:17:15,841 --> 00:17:17,340
This will stop it.

