than what Batman actually has.

476
00:29:40,541 --> 00:29:44,340
Batman's utility belt may be the ultimate in compact crime

477
00:29:44,341 --> 00:29:47,960
fighting, but the caped crusader doesn't always think small.

478
00:29:49,340 --> 00:29:57,120
And Batman tech doesn't get any bigger or cooler than an automobile that's become a pop culture icon.

479
00:29:57,580 --> 00:29:59,820
At least tell me what it looks like.

480
00:30:02,340 --> 00:30:03,180
Never mind.

481
00:30:04,240 --> 00:30:05,140
What's that?

482
00:30:05,920 --> 00:30:06,620
The tumbler?

483
00:30:07,520 --> 00:30:09,060
Oh, you wouldn't be interested in that.

484
00:30:09,061 --> 00:30:10,060
Batman.

485
00:30:10,061 --> 00:30:23,060
Since 1941, Batman has cruised the streets of Gotham City in a car that pays flashy tribute

486
00:30:23,061 --> 00:30:25,880
to his nocturnal namesake.

487
00:30:25,881 --> 00:30:32,360
But whether it's got scalloped fins, a bat's head battering ram, or a jet propelled engine,

488
00:30:32,361 --> 00:30:37,060
the Batmobile may be the most coveted item in all Batman tech.

489
00:30:37,061 --> 00:30:39,960
I think the Batmobile had a major influence on me.

490
00:30:39,961 --> 00:30:41,460
I mean, I was fascinated by it.

491
00:30:41,461 --> 00:30:42,560
I wanted to drive it.

492
00:30:42,561 --> 00:30:43,660
I wanted to see it.

493
00:30:43,661 --> 00:30:47,460
And I think it kind of got me into cars at an early age that way.

494
00:30:47,461 --> 00:30:51,660
Artists and writers have kept improving on the Batmobile's design,

495
00:30:51,661 --> 00:30:55,760
with additions and overhauls reflecting car trends of the day.

496
00:30:55,761 --> 00:30:57,260
You ever-changing Batmobile?

497
00:30:57,261 --> 00:30:59,160
You know, you see a different Batmobile for every year.

498
00:30:59,161 --> 00:31:02,760
You see a different Batmobile for every generation.

499
00:31:02,761 --> 00:31:05,960
In the 40s, you had the big grill, which was kind of cool.

500
00:31:05,961 --> 00:31:09,660
The first Batmobile I remember was the Batmobile of the 50s

501
00:31:09,661 --> 00:31:11,820
with the huge bat fin on the back

502
00:31:11,821 --> 00:31:13,720
and the bat-headed baton ram in the front.

503
00:31:14,040 --> 00:31:15,100
It was big enough to be a tank.

504
00:31:15,600 --> 00:31:17,820
Then he got into the 60s and the car evolved

505
00:31:17,821 --> 00:31:19,520
to match the one in the television series

506
00:31:19,521 --> 00:31:20,800
with the atomic turbines.

507
00:31:21,500 --> 00:31:23,880
Then in the early 70s, it became a sports car.

508
00:31:24,080 --> 00:31:25,080
I always thought that was the coolest.

509
00:31:25,520 --> 00:31:28,200
I mean, the whole idea that this singular unique vehicle

510
00:31:28,201 --> 00:31:30,380
belongs to a singular unique character.

511
00:31:32,440 --> 00:31:33,500
So what do you think?

512
00:31:34,120 --> 00:31:35,560
Does it come in black?

513
00:31:35,960 --> 00:31:40,960
As Batman's enemies got tougher, so did his car.

514
00:31:41,960 --> 00:31:42,960
Make a color.

515
00:31:42,961 --> 00:31:45,960
That's a black... tank.

516
00:31:45,961 --> 00:31:51,960
And no retooling of the Batmobile was more radical than the one showcased in Batman Begins.

517
00:31:51,961 --> 00:31:52,960
Hold on.

518
00:31:53,960 --> 00:32:00,960
Director Christopher Nolan and designer Nathan Crowley set out to create a 21st century ride.

519
00:32:00,961 --> 00:32:03,960
One whose practicality and power...

520
00:32:03,961 --> 00:32:06,960
...would help set the tone for the entire film.

521
00:32:06,961 --> 00:32:11,960
The purpose of redesigning the Batmobile, which we call the Tumbler...

522
00:32:11,961 --> 00:32:15,960
...was to have it have capabilities that we felt a crime fighter...

523
00:32:15,961 --> 00:32:18,960
...would need to have in the modern day.

524
00:32:21,960 --> 00:32:24,960
The Tumbler was the first thing we designed...

525
00:32:24,961 --> 00:32:27,960
...because I felt that if we could show the studio...

526
00:32:27,961 --> 00:32:30,800
what the Batmobile was in our world,

527
00:32:30,801 --> 00:32:33,560
they'd get a handle on what everything else would be.

528
00:32:33,561 --> 00:32:35,000
Action!

529
00:32:35,001 --> 00:32:37,600
I felt that we needed a new contemporary approach

530
00:32:37,601 --> 00:32:40,640
in order to believe in the utility of this vehicle.

531
00:32:40,641 --> 00:32:44,440
So what I proposed was a cross between a Lamborghini and a Humvee,

532
00:32:44,441 --> 00:32:47,920
something that would have the presence of almost a tank-like vehicle,

533
00:32:47,921 --> 00:32:51,480
but also with the speed and grace of a sports car.

534
00:32:52,760 --> 00:32:54,920
She was built as a bridging vehicle.

535
00:32:54,921 --> 00:33:01,920
During combat, two of these would jump over a river towing cables.

536
00:33:01,921 --> 00:33:14,920
So by definition, it needed to have a jet engine in it to allow it to jump over rivers or whatever in order to take the equipment across.

537
00:33:14,921 --> 00:33:21,920
It needed to have armor to protect it from taking hits.

538
00:33:21,921 --> 00:33:22,621
hits.

539
00:33:22,622 --> 00:33:31,560
Also has the ability to drive in a stealth mode with an engine that's incredibly quiet

540
00:33:31,561 --> 00:33:35,559
so it can sort of disappear into the environment.

541
00:33:35,560 --> 00:33:38,660
It's a pretty cool piece of equipment.

542
00:33:39,180 --> 00:33:44,920
The tumbler seems surprisingly realistic, but how much of it would actually work?

543
00:33:45,620 --> 00:33:47,300
Let's start with the aerodynamics.

544
00:33:48,020 --> 00:33:53,620
In spite of its weight of about 5,000 pounds, the tumbler can achieve impressive speed.

545
00:33:53,621 --> 00:34:02,540
The tumbler is a big, bulky, tank-like machine, but probably can go about 120, 130 miles an hour.

546
00:34:02,920 --> 00:34:06,040
Credit goes to its surprisingly sleek design.

547
00:34:06,740 --> 00:34:14,800
Just as airplane flaps generate lift to make a plane go up, the tumbler uses flaps to push the vehicle down.

548
00:34:14,920 --> 00:34:16,820
and achieve greater velocity.

549
00:34:17,180 --> 00:34:21,420
The theory behind it is that it's got all these little aerofoils on the outside

550
00:34:21,421 --> 00:34:26,300
that all make tiny little wings instead of having one big as an aircraft.

551
00:34:26,620 --> 00:34:31,060
The other key aerodynamic element, surprisingly, is the airflow under the car.

552
00:34:31,620 --> 00:34:33,560
And this is actually what racing cars use.

553
00:34:34,020 --> 00:34:38,840
If you can design that air under the car to go significantly faster than the air on the top of the car,

554
00:34:38,841 --> 00:34:43,960
you get low pressure under the car, and the high pressure on top pushes you down on the ground.

555
00:34:43,961 --> 00:34:49,200
So if you want to understand how the tumbler gains stability by having the air blow underneath it,

556
00:34:49,201 --> 00:34:54,160
you can just take a piece of paper, you can generate high pressure on top and a low pressure underneath

557
00:34:54,161 --> 00:34:57,320
by blowing under the paper, and the paper will be forced down.

558
00:35:01,060 --> 00:35:06,780
Speed is one thing, but how does something as large as the tumbler manage to maneuver so well?

559
00:35:07,440 --> 00:35:09,800
Weight does have a great effect on maneuverability.

560
00:35:10,280 --> 00:35:12,080
You have all this mass you have to move around.

561
00:35:12,081 --> 00:35:14,620
It's transmitted through the wheels and tires to the road.

562
00:35:15,020 --> 00:35:17,440
Really, you've got to hand it to the designers automotive-wise.

563
00:35:17,620 --> 00:35:18,760
It's quite a feat of engineering.

564
00:35:18,880 --> 00:35:21,920
They seem to have each wheel as kind of balanced out by itself

565
00:35:21,921 --> 00:35:23,860
without an axle running across the middle.

566
00:35:24,240 --> 00:35:25,920
Both wheels are totally independent,

567
00:35:26,080 --> 00:35:29,760
so one wheel can actually stop and the other wheel can rotate

568
00:35:29,761 --> 00:35:31,440
so the thing turns right on a dime.

569
00:35:31,680 --> 00:35:33,100
And it can do that at any speed.

570
00:35:33,340 --> 00:35:34,660
That's what's so amazing about it.

571
00:35:36,800 --> 00:35:38,560
I've got to get me one of those.

572
00:35:38,561 --> 00:35:44,100
The Tumbler is designed to get some of its momentum from a jet-powered engine,

573
00:35:44,700 --> 00:35:46,880
another detail rooted in reality.

574
00:35:47,680 --> 00:35:50,900
Jet-powered cars have been used to set land speed records,

575
00:35:51,120 --> 00:35:54,420
and they've even made brief trips into the consumer world.

576
00:35:54,700 --> 00:35:57,180
They've tried to use jet engines in cars throughout history.

577
00:35:57,640 --> 00:36:00,400
In 1963, Chrysler introduced the turbine car.

578
00:36:00,920 --> 00:36:03,700
Fifty models they made had a jet engine in it.

579
00:36:04,040 --> 00:36:07,320
They only gave them to about 200 customers for three months each.

580
00:36:07,321 --> 00:36:09,220
It was a very experimental program.

581
00:36:09,221 --> 00:36:11,120
Most people who drove it loved it.

582
00:36:11,121 --> 00:36:13,960
Unfortunately, the car wasn't great on gas mileage.

583
00:36:13,961 --> 00:36:20,440
It's a very complicated car, and it kind of died a few years later.

584
00:36:20,441 --> 00:36:24,340
Over here on the throttle, flip that open and throttle up.

585
00:36:24,341 --> 00:36:26,280
This will boost you into a rampless jump.

586
00:36:30,240 --> 00:36:35,480
On screen, the tumbler can also make unassisted or rampless jumps.

587
00:36:35,481 --> 00:36:38,140
If it comes off perfectly parallel to the ground,

588
00:36:38,141 --> 00:36:40,280
it's always going to fall a little bit.

589
00:36:40,281 --> 00:36:42,120
And so if it's jumping to something that's a little bit

590
00:36:42,121 --> 00:36:43,720
lower, it's OK.

591
00:36:43,721 --> 00:36:46,920
If it wants to jump to something at the same height or higher,

592
00:36:46,921 --> 00:36:48,820
it needs some form of lift or it needs

593
00:36:48,821 --> 00:36:50,120
to come off at a slight angle.

594
00:36:54,760 --> 00:36:56,940
The way you could do this is imagine a little bit of a wheelie

595
00:36:56,941 --> 00:36:58,000
as you take off.

596
00:36:58,001 --> 00:36:59,780
You don't actually need a ramp to get a little bit

597
00:36:59,781 --> 00:37:02,200
of vertical velocity, especially since you've

598
00:37:02,201 --> 00:37:05,280
got the jet engine on the back to give you that extra thrust.

599
00:37:05,281 --> 00:37:07,120
You just get the front end of the car up a little bit,

600
00:37:07,121 --> 00:37:09,460
fire your jet engine, and now you're going off at an angle.

601
00:37:14,920 --> 00:37:18,220
We were confident that we could do some pretty amazing jumps,

602
00:37:18,221 --> 00:37:19,500
and it land and drive off.

603
00:37:19,501 --> 00:37:22,100
You know, not the classic thing where the car jumps,

604
00:37:22,101 --> 00:37:25,200
lands, falls apart, and then you cut and put another car in

605
00:37:25,201 --> 00:37:26,140
and drive away.

606
00:37:26,141 --> 00:37:28,460
We were proud of the fact that we could do all that

607
00:37:28,461 --> 00:37:30,680
and still carry on the seasons.

608
00:37:30,681 --> 00:37:33,980
If you had powerful enough hydraulics or electromagnetic

609
00:37:33,981 --> 00:37:37,860
shots up front and then you had a very powerful jet engine that aimed down a little bit, you

610
00:37:37,861 --> 00:37:42,020
might be able to get enough of a leaping effect to go 10, 20, 30 feet in the air.

611
00:37:42,360 --> 00:37:46,208
The real danger is the landing. He's going to be landing at a very high speed.

612
00:37:46,209 --> 00:37:46,909
So the front

613
00:37:46,910 --> 00:37:50,627
end of the car has to have the stability and the shock system to survive that jump.

614
00:37:50,628 --> 00:37:51,328
And in fact,

615
00:37:51,329 --> 00:37:54,059
if you look closely, the Batmobile does some interesting thing.

616
00:37:54,060 --> 00:37:55,140
The front wheels extend,

617
00:37:55,500 --> 00:37:59,600
there's extra shock absorbers there, and when it hits the ground, it slows down over that longer

618
00:37:59,601 --> 00:38:01,640
distance that enables it to survive the impact.

619
00:38:03,980 --> 00:38:07,320
The Batmobile Tumbler is certainly impressive,

620
00:38:07,360 --> 00:38:09,560
but the tech team at Wayne Enterprises

621
00:38:09,580 --> 00:38:12,420
isn't resting on its automotive laurels.

622
00:38:12,460 --> 00:38:16,720
These days, Batman's got a new and even more outrageous way

623
00:38:16,760 --> 00:38:20,300
to navigate the mean streets of Gotham City.

624
00:38:23,060 --> 00:38:28,940
The prehistoric world transforms into a battlefield.

625
00:38:33,980 --> 00:38:41,060
In this place, there's only one rule.

626
00:38:41,061 --> 00:38:42,740
Survive.

627
00:38:43,860 --> 00:38:49,540
Jurassic Fight Club, a new series, premieres July 29th at 9, only on History.

628
00:38:52,220 --> 00:38:54,180
Will you be wanting the Batpod, sir?

629
00:38:54,280 --> 00:38:56,120
In the middle of the day, Alfred? Not very subtle.

630
00:38:56,380 --> 00:38:57,320
The Lamborghini, then.

631
00:38:59,500 --> 00:39:00,580
Much more subtle.

632
00:39:00,581 --> 00:39:05,220
Over the years, Batman has used his technological know-how

633
00:39:05,221 --> 00:39:09,560
to create countless vehicles to help him fight enemies like the Joker.

634
00:39:10,820 --> 00:39:15,620
He's had bat planes, bat boats, bat copters,

635
00:39:15,940 --> 00:39:19,540
and even a vehicle that could go from the air to under the sea.

636
00:39:21,600 --> 00:39:24,180
Three years after Batman Begins,

637
00:39:24,181 --> 00:39:29,060
its sequel, The Dark Knight, pushed Batman tech even further.

638
00:39:30,580 --> 00:39:40,500
One of the joys of working on a character who's been around for thousands of stories is you have to continually ask, how do I top this?

639
00:39:41,140 --> 00:39:43,600
The answer? The Batpod.

640
00:39:44,120 --> 00:39:48,800
A bold new vehicle that's part motorcycle and part lethal weapon.

641
00:39:49,340 --> 00:39:56,980
It's something which looks like some crazy Viking's idea of a customized motorbike.

642
00:39:56,981 --> 00:40:01,720
It looks formidable and like everything with the movie, it works.

643
00:40:05,920 --> 00:40:08,400
It looks raw and it looks very extreme.

644
00:40:08,800 --> 00:40:10,400
It looks really powerful and dangerous.

645
00:40:10,660 --> 00:40:13,760
So I think that is sort of the bad boy, you know?

646
00:40:18,500 --> 00:40:19,440
Bad man.

647
00:40:21,840 --> 00:40:25,800
The task, as usual, was to build something that could really go fast,

648
00:40:25,801 --> 00:40:31,600
make turns, you know, the usual outrageous, you know, parameters.

649
00:40:32,300 --> 00:40:35,080
It really had to belong to the same family as the Batmobile,

650
00:40:35,420 --> 00:40:36,880
so that's where we started.

651
00:40:38,580 --> 00:40:41,440
I'd hesitate to even call this a motorcycle

652
00:40:41,441 --> 00:40:45,240
just because it's so different from the way a motorcycle typically handles.

653
00:40:45,360 --> 00:40:46,740
I mean, there isn't really a seat.

654
00:40:46,860 --> 00:40:48,100
You're lying down on your belly,

655
00:40:48,101 --> 00:40:50,860
and your legs are splayed apart three and a half feet.

656
00:40:51,360 --> 00:40:54,320
Riding the Batpod in a practically prone position

657
00:40:54,321 --> 00:40:57,280
gives the Dark Knight an aerodynamic edge.

658
00:40:57,760 --> 00:41:01,720
The low-profile technique is frequently used by professional racers.

659
00:41:02,320 --> 00:41:04,880
Grand Prix motorcycle racers, whenever they get a chance,

660
00:41:04,980 --> 00:41:06,680
whenever they're on a straightaway, they duck down

661
00:41:06,681 --> 00:41:09,160
and they make themselves as small as possible.

662
00:41:09,820 --> 00:41:11,820
And it's that aerodynamic drag they're trying to eliminate.

663
00:41:12,260 --> 00:41:15,080
When Batman is down on the Batpod in that position,

664
00:41:15,480 --> 00:41:17,900
he's eliminating drag and he's a lot less exposed.

665
00:41:17,901 --> 00:41:19,900
And he's also lowering the center of gravity

666
00:41:19,901 --> 00:41:21,460
so he has more control over the vehicle.

667
00:41:21,461 --> 00:41:25,460
The Batpod weighs about 700 pounds.

668
00:41:25,461 --> 00:41:29,460
Because it's so large, controlling the bike takes extra skill,

669
00:41:29,461 --> 00:41:33,460
including the use of special handlebars, which act as arm shields.

670
00:41:33,461 --> 00:41:36,460
The steering of it was totally unconventional.

671
00:41:36,461 --> 00:41:40,460
You had these big cowls that came around his arms.

672
00:41:40,461 --> 00:41:43,460
It was more from his shoulder, actually, that he steered.

673
00:41:43,461 --> 00:41:46,460
Well, you want to use more of your body weight to turn a bike,

674
00:41:46,461 --> 00:41:47,460
and on this you're going to...

675
00:41:47,461 --> 00:41:52,320
I think that if you're not just using your arms and your hands placed on the handlebar,

676
00:41:52,400 --> 00:41:58,820
but you've got this action so that you're in these arm shields that help you sort of lean the bike in,

677
00:41:58,920 --> 00:42:00,100
that's going to help you maneuver it.

678
00:42:00,180 --> 00:42:04,440
So that you're really forced to use your body weight to control it as opposed to just arms

679
00:42:04,441 --> 00:42:10,260
because you'd have to be Arnold Schwarzenegger in order to be able to turn that kind of tire on a motorcycle.

680
00:42:11,640 --> 00:42:16,560
Besides the way it's steered, the Batpod is also unique in the way it's propelled.

681
00:42:16,561 --> 00:42:21,180
Well, the thing that strikes me the most about this is that where you would expect the motor

682
00:42:21,181 --> 00:42:22,920
to be, it doesn't exist.

683
00:42:22,921 --> 00:42:24,560
It's not in the middle of the bike.

684
00:42:24,561 --> 00:42:29,240
A standard motorcycle has a single engine in the center of the vehicle.

685
00:42:29,241 --> 00:42:34,080
On screen, the Batpod is intended to have not one, but two engines.

686
00:42:34,081 --> 00:42:39,520
And amazingly, one is tucked inside the hub of the bike's front wheel and the other inside

687
00:42:39,521 --> 00:42:40,520
the back wheel.

688
00:42:40,521 --> 00:42:44,840
Putting the engines inside the wheels is being worked on actually by a number of companies

689
00:42:44,841 --> 00:42:45,840
right now.

690
00:42:45,841 --> 00:42:53,980
In 2003, a Swiss engineering team developed a 160 horsepower engine mounted inside 22-inch car tires.

691
00:42:54,920 --> 00:42:59,640
Known as independent wheel drive, the technology can also be used in motorcycles,

692
00:43:00,120 --> 00:43:03,560
though it works best when the engine is in just one wheel of the bike.

693
00:43:04,140 --> 00:43:09,400
The disadvantage to having an engine in both wheels is that they have to be synchronized some way.

694
00:43:09,700 --> 00:43:14,040
Otherwise, if one's spinning faster than the other, of course, one's trying to push you too fast

695
00:43:14,041 --> 00:43:15,520
or the other one's trying to pull you too fast.

696
00:43:15,840 --> 00:43:17,520
They would have to have computer control.

697
00:43:18,600 --> 00:43:20,640
This is something Batman, of course, can afford,

698
00:43:20,840 --> 00:43:23,020
and he would have his perfectly synchronized,

699
00:43:23,240 --> 00:43:24,600
and that way he's got great traction

700
00:43:24,601 --> 00:43:26,760
because he's got engine putting power down in back,

701
00:43:27,100 --> 00:43:29,500
engine putting power down in front, all synchronized.

702
00:43:29,740 --> 00:43:30,440
He's good to go.

703
00:43:39,660 --> 00:43:42,820
Today, thanks to scientists and engineers

704
00:43:42,821 --> 00:43:46,060
who've been inspired by the gadgets in the Dark Knight's world,

705
00:43:46,560 --> 00:43:50,160
Batman's technology is no longer just fantasy.

706
00:44:00,640 --> 00:44:03,560
I think much of the technology that comes out of Batman

707
00:44:03,561 --> 00:44:06,900
comes out of people who were fans,

708
00:44:07,040 --> 00:44:10,300
who are now scientists, inventors, designers.

709
00:44:11,000 --> 00:44:12,300
If you're a kid watching this stuff

710
00:44:12,301 --> 00:44:14,460
for reading about it, makes you want to go out there

711
00:44:14,461 --> 00:44:16,480
and try to make things yourself.

712
00:44:16,481 --> 00:44:18,160
It's a seamless loop.

713
00:44:18,161 --> 00:44:21,040
The changes in the real world inspire the writers,

714
00:44:21,041 --> 00:44:23,300
and the writers and the artists, in turn,

715
00:44:23,301 --> 00:44:26,660
inspire the scientists and the engineers to dream.

716
00:44:26,661 --> 00:44:30,940
I've seen now what it has to become to stop men like him.

717
00:44:30,941 --> 00:44:35,880
From high-speed batmobiles to fast-flying Batarang blades,

718
00:44:35,881 --> 00:44:40,720
and from armor-plated bat suits to supercharged grappling

719
00:44:40,721 --> 00:44:45,720
guns, Batman has set the standard for superhero tech.

720
00:44:45,721 --> 00:44:51,040
What I love about Batman is the sense that these things really are possible.

721
00:44:51,041 --> 00:44:55,480
I think that makes him much more relatable because Batman's very much a human being.

722
00:44:55,481 --> 00:45:01,540
He embodies that fantasy of a man who through sheer self-discipline turned himself into

723
00:45:01,541 --> 00:45:03,040
a heroic figure.

724
00:45:03,041 --> 00:45:05,280
I think that's just a very compelling myth.

725
00:45:05,281 --> 00:45:06,560
I never said thank you.

726
00:45:06,561 --> 00:45:08,520
And you'll never have to.

727
00:45:08,521 --> 00:45:11,840
The accessibility of Batman is because you don't have to be rocketed from another planet

728
00:45:11,841 --> 00:45:13,500
or have strange powers.

729
00:45:13,501 --> 00:45:17,620
All you have to be is the top of your physical ability and top of what your mind can achieve

730
00:45:17,621 --> 00:45:19,140
and in doing so you can become Batman.

